<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name = "a" from = "-2" to = "2" step = "1" exclude="0"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "b" from = "2" to = "5" step = "1" exclude="0 $a"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "c" from = "-3" to = "3" step = "1" exclude="0 $a $b"/>

  <selectFromSequence name = "p" from = "0" to = "1" step = "0.2" exclude="0"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "q" from = "2" to = "4" step = "1"/>

  <function name="f" symbolic="false">$a*x*e^(-$b*x) + $c</function>
  <derivative name="fP">$f</derivative>
  <function name="fextrema" domain="[$p,$q]">$f</function>

  <number name="crNum">1/$b</number>

</setup>

<p>
  Consider the function <m>f(x) = <math simplify="numberspreserveorder">$a x e^(-$b x) + $c</math></m> on the interval <m>[$p,$q]</m>. Use calculus to find the exact absolute minimum and absolute maximum of <m>f</m> on this interval.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        For <m>f(x) = <math simplify="numberspreserveorder">$a x e^(-$b x) + $c</math></m>, it follows that 
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer>
          <label>
            <m>f'(x)=</m>
          </label>
          $fP
        </answer>
      </p>
      <p>
        Find all critical numbers of <m>f</m>.  If there is more than one critical number, enter them as a list separated by commas.  If there are none, enter <em>none</em>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><label>The exact critical numbers of <m>f</m> are: <m>x = </m></label>$crNum</answer>
      </p>
      <p>
        Evaluate the function at any critical numbers that lie in the interval <m>[$p,$q]</m>.  If there is more than one such critical number, enter the function values as a list separated by commas.  If there are no critical numbers in the interval <m>[$p,$q]</m>, enter <em>none</em>. (<alert>Note</alert>: to enter exact function values, use notation such as <m>e^{-1}</m>.  If you enter a decimal representation, report your result accurate to 3 decimal places.)
      </p>
      <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label>The value(s) of <m>f</m> at any applicable critical numbers are:</label>
        <conditionalContent>
          <case condition="$crNum>= $p and $crNum<= $q">$$f($crNum)</case>
          <else>none</else>
        </conditionalContent>
      </answer>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        The values of the function at the respective endpoints of the interval are:
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label><m>f($p) =</m></label>$$f($p)</answer> and <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label><m>f($q) =</m></label>$$f($q)</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label>The absolute minimum value of <m>f</m> on <m>[$p,$q]</m> is </label>$fextrema.globalMinimum[2]</answer>
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label>The absolute maximum value of <m>f</m> on <m>[$p,$q]</m> is </label>$fextrema.globalMaximum[2]</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>